    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d408">

                <pb facs="0519" n="447" xml:id="pg447"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 22372/1.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Nicaraguan
                    Chargé.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1909-11-18"><hi rendition="#italic">November 18,
                        1909</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to request you, as the
                    diplomatic channel of communication between the Government of the United States
                    and that of President Zelaya, immediately to telegraph to that Government that
                    the Government of the United States can scarcely believe the report that two
                    Americans captured with the revolutionary army of Gen. Estrada have been
                    summarily executed, and that if this grievous report be true the Government of
                    the United States demands instant information of all the particulars, meanwhile
                    reserving for future decision the measures to be taken in such an
                    eventuality.</p>
                <p>You will readily appreciate the urgency of this matter as well as its
                    determinative bearing upon further relations between this Government and that
                    which you represent.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">P. C. Knox.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
